John H. <JohnWH@gmail.com> wrote:
> Pasi Kallinen wrote:
>> This patch fixes one of my main pet peeves: Falling through trapdoors
>> takes you to a random location.
> 
> What happens if a boulder or pool is on the spot where a
> previously-determined hole leads?  How about a stone wall (is that
> possible)?  Or a monster?

the goodpos() function (from teleport.c) is used to see if the location
is valid. If not, then we choose another location close to it.
If no good place is found, then the player could end up in
a stone wall.

There's definitely some room for improvement in the patch, such as
handling the special level exceptions, and trying harder to find
a good pos to land the player.

